  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Write path contract",
      "items": [
        "Every commerce function: claim key -> validate -> business row -> outbox envelope -> record response -> commit, in one session.",
        "A failed request rolls the idempotency row back with the transaction, so a retry can still succeed.",
        "The API never writes ledger rows; the bill travels inside the event payload."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Handler contract",
      "items": [
        "_claim commits a lease (locked_until = now + 300 s) before any side effect; a concurrent delivery raises EventInProgressError and the SQS message is left alone.",
        "The receipt is stored write-once before the handler transaction; ledger + stats + derived outbox row + attempt=succeeded commit together.",
        "Terminal failure uses the durable attempt_number (>= 5), never the SQS receive count."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Modules drawn as types",
      "items": [
        "services.commerce, services.idempotency and services.outbox are Python modules of functions, drawn as types to show the call structure.",
        "Replay, CommerceResult, _Claim, _SourceEvent, _Receipt, ProcessResult, PollResult and ConsumeResult are small frozen dataclasses omitted for space."
      ]
    }
  ]
}